    sections: [
      { title: 'Comprehensive Resource Quantification & Assessment', content: 'Modern geological surveys utilizing advanced exploration techniques have fundamentally transformed understanding of Afghanistan\'s mineral wealth. USGS comprehensive assessment in 2010 identified $1-3 trillion in mineral value, with subsequent surveys revealing even greater potential reaching $30+ trillion. Advanced satellite imagery analysis identified surface mineralization indicators across vast areas, while airborne geophysical surveys revealed subsurface geological structures invisible to surface mapping. Deep drilling programs extending to 1,500 meters below surface confirmed deposit continuity and resource estimates. Integration of modern exploration data with historical Soviet surveys created comprehensive mineral resource database documenting world-class deposits across all major categories. The quantification process employed international resource estimation standards, ensuring credibility for investment decisions.' },
      { title: 'Major Discoveries & World-Class Deposits', content: 'Modern exploration has revealed world-class deposits positioning Afghanistan among the world\'s most significant mineral resource nations. Lithium discovery in Ghazni Province represents potentially the world\'s largest reserves with 215 million metric tons of lithium carbonate equivalent—enough to supply global demand for decades. Confirmation of Mes Aynak copper deposit\'s exceptional scale and grade validates its status as one of the world\'s largest undeveloped copper deposits. Hajigak iron deposit confirmation establishes Afghanistan\'s potential as Central Asia\'s steel manufacturing hub. Rare earth element discoveries position Afghanistan as critical supplier for technology sectors. The comprehensive discovery portfolio spans all major mineral categories, creating diversified development opportunities supporting national economic transformation.' },
      { title: 'Investment Frameworks & Development Strategy', content: 'Modern era has established comprehensive investment frameworks enabling systematic mineral development. Transparent licensing procedures, competitive fiscal terms, and international arbitration access attract world-class mining companies. Environmental and social impact assessment requirements ensure sustainable development practices. Community benefit frameworks ensure local populations share in mining benefits through employment, procurement, and community development programs. Infrastructure development plans connect mining regions to global markets through rail, road, and port facilities. The comprehensive development strategy balances rapid resource development with environmental protection, community benefit, and economic diversification. Investment frameworks create confidence for international investors while ensuring Afghanistan maximizes value from mineral development.' },
      { title: 'Technology & Innovation Integration', content: 'Modern mineral development incorporates cutting-edge technology maximizing efficiency and minimizing environmental impact. Autonomous mining equipment improves safety while increasing productivity. Advanced processing technologies maximize recovery rates while reducing energy consumption and environmental footprint. Digital twin technology enables optimization before implementation. Predictive maintenance systems reduce downtime and costs. Renewable energy integration reduces carbon footprint while ensuring reliable power supply. Water recycling systems achieve 95%+ reuse minimizing freshwater consumption. The technology focus positions Afghanistan\'s mining sector at the forefront of sustainable mining practices while maximizing economic returns.' }
    ],
